-- title:
--   Index of a full-rank submodule equals the determinant ideal's index
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a principal ideal ring, let $M$ be an $R$-module (an additive commutative group with an $R$-module structure), and let $\iota$ be a finite index type. Given a basis $b : \iota \to M$ of $M$ over $R$, a submodule $N \subseteq M$, and a basis $bN$ of $N$ indexed by the same type $\iota$ (so that $N$ has full rank in $M$), the assertion is the equality of natural numbers
--   $$\#(M/N) = \#\bigl(R/(d)\bigr), \qquad d = \det{}_b\bigl(i \mapsto bN_i\bigr),$$
--   where $d \in R$ is the determinant, computed in the basis $b$, of the family of images in $M$ of the basis vectors of $N$, $(d)$ denotes the ideal of $R$ generated by the single element $d$, and both cardinalities are taken as `Nat.card`, so that each side is $0$ precisely when the corresponding quotient is infinite. In particular no finiteness of the quotients is assumed; the statement includes the infinite case through this convention.
--
--   This is the determinant formula for the index of a full-rank submodule of a finite free module over a principal ideal domain, generalising Mathlib's integral case `Submodule.natAbs_det_basis_change` ($R = \mathbb{Z}$, where the right-hand side is $|\det|$) to an arbitrary principal ideal domain; over the valuation ring of a non-archimedean local field with residue field of size $q$ it reads $[M : N] = q^{v(d)}$. It is used in the computation of relative indices of spans of lattices over Dedekind domains, via [`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.relIndex_span_range_mul_norm_det_eq_one_of_forall_mem_span`](thm.html#IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.relIndex_span_range_mul_norm_det_eq_one_of_forall_mem_span).
